//! Tables 6-4 to 6-9 of the manual (superelevation rates and minimum runoff lengths), transcribed.
//!
//! Source: Uganda MoWT Road Design Manual Volume I: Geometric Design, January 2010, printed pages 98 to 103
//! (PDF pages 107 to 112). Each table: rows of curve radius R (m) from 7000 down to 30, and for each design
//! speed 30 to 120 km/h a cell of the form NC (normal crown), RC (remove adverse crown, superelevation at the
//! normal crown slope) or a superelevation rate in percent, with the minimum length of runoff L (m, which the
//! manual says does not include the tangent runout). A cell the table leaves empty is `None`: the radius is below
//! the minimum radius the table prints for that speed (the `Rmin` cell). Values were read from the text layer of
//! the PDF and confirmed against the rendered pages; the L column was also recomputed from the manual formula
//! (see the tests in `tests/mowt_horizontal.rs`).
//! Generated once by a transcription script; edit only to correct a transcription error.

